CONCLUSION: Across all methods the ability-adjusted Black completion advantage
grows monotonically with SES and is LARGEST at the TOP SES stratum
(quartile Q4 / quintile Q5). The Black x SES interaction is positive and
statistically significant (coef=0.4805, p=0.012). Point estimates: Q4=+2.01 pp,
Q5=+3.41 pp. CIs are wide (only 28 Black completions), so the significant
interaction is the most reliable evidence; per-stratum estimates are directional.
